    424.08
   ],
   "id": "e9",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.44,
      192.72,
      254.88,
      201.36
     ],
     "text": "All characteristics described are from a comparative"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.44,
      203.52,
      255.36,
      212.4
     ],
     "text": "growing trial conducted at Cressy Research Station, near"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      214.56,
      255.36,
      223.44
     ],
     "text": "Launceston, Tasmania, in 1990 and 1991, 100 spaced"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      225.6,
      254.88,
      234.48
     ],
     "text": "plants of each variety were planted in a randomised com-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      236.64,
      254.88,
      245.76
     ],
     "text": "plete block design with 10 blocks, Each plot contained"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      44.4,
      247.44,
      255.12,
      256.8
     ],
     "text": "10 plants (2 rows x 5 plants) of a particular variety with"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      258.96,
      254.88,
      267.84
     ],
     "text": "a between plant spacing of 60cm. A similar trial was also"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      270.24,
      254.88,
      279.12
     ],
     "text": "planted in 1990 at Cressy Research Station which"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      281.28,
      236.16,
      289.92
     ],
     "text": "included only the varieties \u2018Jackaroo\u2019 and \u2018Roper\u2019."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.44,
      294.72,
      254.88,
      303.84
     ],
     "text": "In addition to evidence of distinctness and stability, the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      306.0,
      254.4,
      314.64
     ],
     "text": "applicant has submitted photographic prints of the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      316.56,
      255.36,
      325.2
     ],
     "text": "results of SDS-polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      43.2,
      327.36,
      254.64,
      336.24
     ],
     "text": "extracted seed protcins. These demonstrate a difference"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      338.4,
      254.64,
      347.28
     ],
     "text": "in banding pattern between the varieties analysed and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.72,
      349.44,
      254.4,
      357.84
     ],
     "text": "consistency between the two samples of \u201cJackaroo\u2019. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      360.0,
      254.4,
      368.88
     ],
     "text": "analytical method used is essentially as described in"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.72,
      371.28,
      254.4,
      379.68
     ],
     "text": "Gardiner, SE and Forde MB (1987), Seed Science and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.72,
      382.32,
      254.4,
      390.96
     ],
     "text": "Technology /5, 663-674, modified by the use of the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.72,
      393.36,
      254.4,
      402.24
     ],
     "text": "extraction medium described by Smith, DB and Payne,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.96,
      404.4,
      254.4,
      413.28
     ],
     "text": "PI (1984), J. natn. Inst. agric. Bot. /6,487-498. The"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      42.72,
      415.44,
      254.4,
      424.08
     ],
     "text": "method is fully described in \u2018Identification of cultivars"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "All characteristics described are from a comparative\ngrowing trial conducted at Cressy Research Station, near\nLaunceston, Tasmania, in 1990 and 1991, 100 spaced\nplants of each variety were planted in a randomised com-\nplete block design with 10 blocks, Each plot contained\n10 plants (2 rows x 5 plants) of a particular variety with\na between plant spacing of 60cm. A similar trial was also\nplanted in 1990 at Cressy Research Station which\nincluded only the varieties \u2018Jackaroo\u2019 and \u2018Roper\u2019.\nIn addition to evidence of distinctness and stability, the\napplicant has submitted photographic prints of the\nresults of SDS-polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis of\nextracted seed protcins. These demonstrate a difference\nin banding pattern between the varieties analysed and\nconsistency between the two samples of \u201cJackaroo\u2019. The\nanalytical method used is essentially as described in\nGardiner, SE and Forde MB (1987), Seed Science and\nTechnology /5, 663-674, modified by the use of the\nextraction medium described by Smith, DB and Payne,\nPI (1984), J. natn. Inst. agric. Bot. /6,487-498. The\nmethod is fully described in \u2018Identification of cultivars",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
